<title>USA: Fed stays out of system during intervention time.</title>
<headline>Fed stays out of system during intervention time.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve stayed out of the money market during its usual midmorning intervention period on Friday, as expected by some economists.</p>
<p>Federal funds were last trading at 5.44 percent, below the Fed's current target of 5.50 percent.</p>
<p>((-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660))</p>
</text>
